<title>SRI LANKA: S.LANKA SAYS TO SET UP THREE NEW INDUSTRIAL PARKS.</title>
<headline>S.LANKA SAYS TO SET UP THREE NEW INDUSTRIAL PARKS.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka plans to set up three new industrial parks in a bid to attract more foreign investment into the country, a senior minister said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Mangala Samaraweera, Minister for Posts, Telecommunication and Media, said land had been identified for the parks in eastern Ampara, northeastern Polonnaruwa and central Kurunegala districts.</p>
<p>The parks are expected to provide more than 5,000 new jobs in these districts, the minister said.</p>
<p>He did not give details of investment for creating infrastructure for the parks or expected foreign investment in them.</p>
</text>
